window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":36,"nomSourate":"Ya-Sin","nomFr":"Ya-Sin","nomEn":"Ya Sin","nomArabe":"يس","lieu":"La Mecque","lieuEn":"Makkah","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateLabelEn":"Meccan Surah","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":41,"nbVersets":83,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ يس","tradPropre":"Yâ Sîn.","tradEn":"Yā, Seen.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Yâ-Sîn: Ces lettres isolées placées en ouverture de la sourate appartiennent au secret d'Allāh et démontrent le miracle inimitable du Coran, composé des mêmes lettres arabes que celles utilisées par les hommes.","explicationEn":"1. Ya Sin. The discussion on similar letters has already passed at the beginning of Sūrah Al-Baqarah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-35-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"وَالْقُرْآنِ الْحَكِيمِ","tradPropre":"Par le Coran plein de sagesse.","tradEn":"By the wise Qur’ān,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah prête serment par le Coran dont les versets sont parfaits et que le faux n’atteint ni par devant ni par derrière.","explicationEn":"2. Allah takes an oath by the Qur’ān, whose verses have been perfectly constructed, and to which no falsehood comes neither from in front of nor behind it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"إِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Tu (Muhammad) es certes du nombre des messagers,","tradEn":"Indeed you, [O Muḥammad], are from among the messengers,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, tu es du nombre des messagers qu’Allah a envoyés à Ses serviteurs afin qu’ils leur ordonnent de proclamer Son Unicité et de L’adorer Seul.","explicationEn":"3. You, O Messenger, are on the messengers whom Allah sent to His servants, to instruct them to declare His Oneness and to worship Him alone.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"عَلَىٰ صِرَاطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ","tradPropre":"sur un chemin droit.","tradEn":"On a straight path.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces messagers suivent un chemin droit. et sont fidèles à une religion authentique révélés par ton Seigneur le Puissant à qui personne ne tient tête, le Miséricordieux avec Ses serviteurs croyants.","explicationEn":"5. This straight approach and upright law is revealed from your Lord, the Mighty, whom no one can challenge, and the Merciful to His servants who have faith.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"تَنْزِيلَ الْعَزِيزِ الرَّحِيمِ","tradPropre":"C'est une révélation de la part du Tout Puissant, du Très Miséricordieux,","tradEn":"[This is] a revelation of the Exalted in Might, the Merciful,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces messagers suivent un chemin droit. et sont fidèles à une religion authentique révélés par ton Seigneur le Puissant à qui personne ne tient tête, le Miséricordieux avec Ses serviteurs croyants.","explicationEn":"5. This straight approach and upright law is revealed from your Lord, the Mighty, whom no one can challenge, and the Merciful to His servants who have faith.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"لِتُنْذِرَ قَوْمًا مَا أُنْذِرَ آبَاؤُهُمْ فَهُمْ غَافِلُونَ","tradPropre":"pour que tu avertisses un peuple dont les ancêtres n'ont pas été avertis: ils sont donc insouciants.","tradEn":"That you may warn a people whose forefathers were not warned, so they are unaware.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous t’avons révélé ceci afin que tu menaces et avertisses un peuple, le peuple des Arabes, qu’aucun messager n’a averti auparavant. Ils sont donc inattentifs à la foi et au monothéisme, ce qui est le cas de tout peuple qui n’a jamais été averti: ce peuple nécessite des messagers pour lui faire le rappel.","explicationEn":"6. I revealed it to you to warn and exhort a nation, the Arabs to whom no Messenger has come to warn them and as a result they are heedless of faith and monotheism. Likewise is the case of every nation which has been away from the exhortation, they need messengers, scholars and preachers to remind them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"لَقَدْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ عَلَىٰ أَكْثَرِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ","tradPropre":"En effet, la Parole contre la plupart d'entre eux s'est réalisée: ils ne croiront donc pas.","tradEn":"Already the word [i.e., decree] has come into effect upon most of them, so they do not believe.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le châtiment d’Allah s’abattra sans appel sur la plupart de ces gens, après que la vérité de la part d’Allah leur sera parvenue par l’intermédiaire de Son Messager, qu’ils n’y auront pas cru et qu’ils resteront mécréants. Ils ne croient donc pas en Allah et en Son Messager et ne mettent pas en pratique la vérité qui leur est parvenue.","explicationEn":"7. The punishment from Allah has become binding on most of these people, after the truth from Allah on the tongue of His Messenger reached them but they did not believe in it and remained on their disbelief. They do not have faith in Allah and nor His Messenger and they do not act on the truth that came to them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا جَعَلْنَا فِي أَعْنَاقِهِمْ أَغْلَالًا فَهِيَ إِلَى الْأَذْقَانِ فَهُمْ مُقْمَحُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous mettrons des carcans à leurs cous, et il y en aura jusqu'aux mentons: et voilà qu'ils iront têtes dressées.","tradEn":"Indeed, We have put shackles on their necks, and they are to their chins, so they are with heads [kept] aloft.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces gens sont semblables à ceux à qui on a mis des carcans au cou et joint les mains au cou en-dessous des mentons. Pris de cette manière, ils sont contraints de lever la tête vers le Ciel sans pouvoir la baisser. Ces gens-là sont privés de croire en Allah et ne se soumettent pas à Lui ni ne baissent la tête devant Lui.","explicationEn":"8. These people do not have faith nor are they guided. Their example in this is like those in whose necks iron collars that extend all the way up and whose hands are tied to their necks under their chins. As a result, they are forced to lift their heads to the sky and they are unable to lower them. These people are shackled from having faith in Allah and therefore they do not submit to it and they do not lower their heads on account of it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلْنَا مِنْ بَيْنِ أَيْدِيهِمْ سَدًّا وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ سَدًّا فَأَغْشَيْنَاهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُبْصِرُونَ","tradPropre":"et Nous mettrons une barrière devant eux et une barrière derrière eux; Nous les recouvrirons d'un voile: et voilà qu'ils ne pourront rien voir.","tradEn":"And We have put before them a barrier and behind them a barrier and covered them, so they do not see.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous mettrons devant eux et derrière eux une barrière qui les empêchera d’atteindre la vérité et Nous voilerons leur vue de telle manière qu’ils ne s’en serviront pas à leur profit. Ceci leur arrivera lorsque s’avèreront leur entêtement et leur persistance dans la mécréance.","explicationEn":"9. I placed before them a barrier to the truth and behind them another barrier. I covered their eyes from the truth so they cannot see in a manner that is of benefit to them. This happened to them after their stubborness and persistence in disbelief became apparent.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"وَسَوَاءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ أَأَنْذَرْتَهُمْ أَمْ لَمْ تُنْذِرْهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Cela leur est égal que tu les avertisses ou que tu ne les avertisses pas: ils ne croiront jamais.","tradEn":"And it is all the same for them whether you warn them or do not warn them - they will not believe.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il est égal à ces mécréants qui rejettent obstinément la vérité, que tu les menaces ou que tu ne les menaces pas, ô Muħammad. Ils ne croiront jamais en ce que tu apportes de la part d’Allah.","explicationEn":"10. It is all the same to these disbelievers who oppose the truth, whether you, O Muhammad, warn them or you do not warn them. They will not accept what you have brought from Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"إِنَّمَا تُنْذِرُ مَنِ اتَّبَعَ الذِّكْرَ وَخَشِيَ الرَّحْمَانَ بِالْغَيْبِ  فَبَشِّرْهُ بِمَغْفِرَةٍ وَأَجْرٍ كَرِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Tu avertis seulement celui qui suit le Rappel (le Coran), et craint le Tout Miséricordieux, malgré qu'il ne Le voit pas. Annonce-lui un pardon et une récompense généreuse.","tradEn":"You can only warn one who follows the message and fears the Most Merciful unseen. So give him good tidings of forgiveness and noble reward.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Celui qui tire véritablement profit de ton avertissement est celui qui croit en ce Coran, suit ce qu’il contient et craint Allah lorsqu’il est seul et que personne d’autre que Lui ne le voit. Annonce à ceux qui possèdent ces caractéristiques, qu’Allah effacera leurs péchés et les leur pardonnera et qu’Il leur réserve une rétribution immense dans l’au-delà qui est le Paradis.","explicationEn":"11. The person who really benefits from your warning is the one who accepts this Qur’ān and follows what is contained in it, and who fears His Lord in solitude where nobody else sees him. So tell those who have these attributes the pleasing news of Allah’s wiping out their sins and HForgiving them and of a great reward awaiting them in the Hereafter, which is entry into Paradise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا نَحْنُ نُحْيِي الْمَوْتَىٰ وَنَكْتُبُ مَا قَدَّمُوا وَآثَارَهُمْ  وَكُلَّ شَيْءٍ أَحْصَيْنَاهُ فِي إِمَامٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"C'est Nous qui ressuscitons les morts et écrivons ce qu'ils ont fait [pour l'au-delà] ainsi que leurs traces. Et Nous avons dénombré toute chose dans un registre explicite.","tradEn":"Indeed, it is We who bring the dead to life and record what they have put forth and what they left behind, and all things We have enumerated in a clear register.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les conséquences, bonnes ou mauvaises, de leurs actes accomplis de leur vivant sont enregistrées même après leur mort.","explicationUnanime":"C’est Nous qui faisons revivre les morts afin de leur faire rendre des comptes le Jour de la Résurrection et Nous consignerons leurs bonnes œuvres comme leurs mauvaises. De même, Nous continuerons à consigner après leur mort les œuvres qui continueront à leur rapporter de bonnes ou de mauvaises actions, comme les aumônes continues ou les actes de mécréance. Nous avons consigné toute chose dans un Livre clair qui est la Table Préservée.","explicationEn":"12. I shall bring the dead back to life by resurrecting them to give account on the day of resurrection. we record the good and the bad deeds that they send forth in this life to be rewarded for in the next, and we also record the good and bad aftereffects from their actions, such as the good that comes out of charity after they pass away and the evils that result of their misdeeds. We have counted everything, and recorded it in a clear book, which is the preserved tablet.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"وَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ مَثَلًا أَصْحَابَ الْقَرْيَةِ إِذْ جَاءَهَا الْمُرْسَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Donne-leur comme exemple les habitants de la cité, quand lui vinrent les envoyés.","tradEn":"And present to them an example: the people of the city, when the messengers came to it -","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Antioche à laquelle se sont présentés les apôtres envoyés par Jésus, selon la majorité des exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, mentionne à ces dénégateurs entêtés un exemple à méditer, celui des habitants de la cité lorsque leurs messagers arrivèrent chez eux.","explicationEn":"13. Give, O Messenger, these stubborn deniers an example that will be a lesson for them, which is the story of the people of the town when their messengers came to them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"إِذْ أَرْسَلْنَا إِلَيْهِمُ اثْنَيْنِ فَكَذَّبُوهُمَا فَعَزَّزْنَا بِثَالِثٍ فَقَالُوا إِنَّا إِلَيْكُمْ مُرْسَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Quand Nous leur envoyâmes deux [envoyés] et qu'ils les traitèrent de menteurs. Nous [les] renforçâmes alors par un troisième et ils dirent: «Vraiment, nous sommes envoyés à vous».","tradEn":"When We sent to them two but they denied them, so We strengthened [them] with a third, and they said, \"Indeed, we are messengers to you.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque Nous leur avons envoyé deux messagers afin de les appeler à proclamer l’Unicité d’Allah et à L’adorer, ils les démentirent et Nous les renforçâmes alors par un troisième. Les trois messagers dirent aux habitants de la cité: Nous trois avons été envoyés afin de vous appeler à proclamer l’Unicité d’Allah et à pratiquer Sa religion.","explicationEn":"14. When I sent to them at first two messengers to call them to Allah’s Oneness and His worship. But they rejected these two messengers. Then we sent as reinforcement for these two a third Messenger with them. The three messengers said to the people of the town: We - all three of us - have been sent to you, to call you to Allah’s Oneness and to follow His law.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا مَا أَنْتُمْ إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِثْلُنَا وَمَا أَنْزَلَ الرَّحْمَانُ مِنْ شَيْءٍ إِنْ أَنْتُمْ إِلَّا تَكْذِبُونَ","tradPropre":"Mais ils [les gens] dirent: «Vous n'êtes que des hommes comme nous. Le Tout Miséricordieux n'a rien fait descendre et vous ne faites que mentir».","tradEn":"They said, \"You are not but human beings like us, and the Most Merciful has not revealed a thing. You are only telling lies.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les habitants de la cité dirent aux messagers: Vous n’êtes que des êtres humains comme nous qui ne nous surpassez par aucun mérite. Par ailleurs, le Tout Miséricordieux ne vous a fait aucune révélation et vous ne faites que mentir sur Allah lorsque vous prétendez cela.","explicationEn":"15. The people of the town said to those who were sent: You are only men like us. You do not have any special status over us. The Merciful has not sent down any revelation to you. You are only lying about Allah in this claim of yours.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا رَبُّنَا يَعْلَمُ إِنَّا إِلَيْكُمْ لَمُرْسَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils [les messagers] dirent: «Notre Seigneur sait qu'en vérité nous sommes envoyés à vous,","tradEn":"They said, \"Our Lord knows that we are messengers to you,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les trois messagers répondirent au démenti des habitants de la cité en ces termes: Ô habitants de la cité, notre Seigneur sait que nous vous avons été envoyés par Lui et ceci suffit comme argument plaidant en notre faveur.","explicationEn":"16. The three messengers said in response to the denial by the people of the town: Our Lord knows that we have been sent by Him to you, O people of the town! That is enough evidence for us.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"وَمَا عَلَيْنَا إِلَّا الْبَلَاغُ الْمُبِينُ","tradPropre":"et il ne nous incombe que de transmettre clairement (notre message)».","tradEn":"And we are not responsible except for clear notification.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il ne nous appartient que de transmettre avec clarté ce qui nous a été ordonné de transmettre. Nous n’avons pas le pouvoir de vous guider.","explicationEn":"17. Our duty is only to clearly convey what we have been instructed to convey to you. We have no control over your guidance.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا إِنَّا تَطَيَّرْنَا بِكُمْ  لَئِنْ لَمْ تَنْتَهُوا لَنَرْجُمَنَّكُمْ وَلَيَمَسَّنَّكُمْ مِنَّا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Nous voyons en vous un mauvais présage. Si vous ne cessez pas, nous vous lapiderons et un douloureux châtiment de notre part vous touchera».","tradEn":"They said, \"Indeed, we consider you a bad omen. If you do not desist, we will surely stone you, and there will surely touch you, from us, a painful punishment.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les habitants de la cité dirent aux messagers: Nous voyons en vous un présage funeste et si vous ne cessez pas de nous inviter au monothéisme, nous vous punirons en vous lapidant jusqu’à ce que mort s’ensuive et nous vous ferons subir un châtiment douloureux.","explicationEn":"18. The people of the town said to the messengers: We see an evil omen in you. If you do not stop calling us to monotheism, we will punish you by stoning to death and you will receive a painful punishment from us.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا طَائِرُكُمْ مَعَكُمْ  أَئِنْ ذُكِّرْتُمْ  بَلْ أَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ مُسْرِفُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Votre mauvais présage est avec vous-mêmes. Est-ce que (c'est ainsi que vous agissez) quand on vous [le] rappelle? Mais vous êtes des gens outranciers!»","tradEn":"They said, \"Your omen [i.e., fate] is with yourselves. Is it because you were reminded? Rather, you are a transgressing people.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les messagers leur répondirent: Le présage funeste est de votre côté puisque vous mécroyez en Allah et vous refusez de suivre Ses messagers. Est-ce en invoquant le mauvais présage que vous répondez lorsqu’on vous rappelle Allah? Vous êtes plutôt des gens qui outrepassez les limites de la mécréance et des péchés.","explicationEn":"19. The messengers said in response to them: Your evil omen is within yourselves on account of your denial of Allah and your leaving out following His messengers. Do you see an evil omen if we reminded you of Allah! In fact, you are a people who have gone too far in the perpetration of disbelief and sins.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"وَجَاءَ مِنْ أَقْصَى الْمَدِينَةِ رَجُلٌ يَسْعَىٰ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اتَّبِعُوا الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Et du bout de la ville, un homme vint en toute hâte et dit: «O mon peuple, suivez les messagers:","tradEn":"And there came from the farthest end of the city a man, running. He said, \"O my people, follow the messengers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"D’une partie éloignée de la ville, vint d’un pas précipité un homme qui redoutait le sort réservé à son peuple pour avoir traité de menteurs les messagers et les avoir menacés de mort et de persécution. Il dit aux siens: Ô mon peuple, suivez ce que ces messagers ont apporté.","explicationEn":"20. From a far part of the town a man came running fearing his people’s denial of the messengers and their threatening to kill or harm them. He said: O my people! Follow what these messengers have brought.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"اتَّبِعُوا مَنْ لَا يَسْأَلُكُمْ أَجْرًا وَهُمْ مُهْتَدُونَ","tradPropre":"suivez ceux qui ne vous demandent aucun salaire et qui sont sur la bonne voie.","tradEn":"Follow those who do not ask of you [any] payment, and they are [rightly] guided.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô mon peuple, suivez ceux qui ne vous demandent aucune récompense et qui sont guidés lorsqu’ils vous transmettent la Révélation d’Allah. Quiconque est ainsi, mérite bien sûr d’être suivi.","explicationEn":"21. O people! Follow those who do not ask you for any reward for conveying what they brought and they are rightly guided in the revelation of Allah that they convey to you. A person like this deserves to be followed.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"وَمَا لِيَ لَا أَعْبُدُ الَّذِي فَطَرَنِي وَإِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ","tradPropre":"et qu'aurais-je à ne pas adorer Celui qui m'a créé? Et c'est vers Lui que vous serez ramenés.","tradEn":"And why should I not worship He who created me and to whom you will be returned?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cet homme, bon conseiller, dit: Que m’empêche-t-il d’adorer Allah qui me créa? Et vous, que vous empêche-t-il d’adorer votre Seigneur qui vous créa et auprès de qui seul vous serez ressuscités et vous rendrez des comptes.","explicationEn":"22. This well-wishing man said: What prevents me from worshipping Allah Who created me? What prevents you from worshipping your Lord Who created you, and to Him alone you will return when you are resurrected for the recompense?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"أَأَتَّخِذُ مِنْ دُونِهِ آلِهَةً إِنْ يُرِدْنِ الرَّحْمَانُ بِضُرٍّ لَا تُغْنِ عَنِّي شَفَاعَتُهُمْ شَيْئًا وَلَا يُنْقِذُونِ","tradPropre":"Prendrais-je en dehors de Lui des divinités? Si le Tout Miséricordieux me veut du mal, leur intercession de me servira à rien et ils ne me sauveront pas.","tradEn":"Should I take other than Him [false] deities [while], if the Most Merciful intends for me some adversity, their intercession will not avail me at all, nor can they save me?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Adopterai-je sans droit des divinités en dehors d’Allah qui m’a créé? Si le Tout Miséricordieux me voulait du mal, l’intercession de ces divinités ne me serait d’aucune utilité car elles n’ont aucun pouvoir de m’être utile ou de me nuire et elles ne peuvent me sauver d’un mal qu’Allah me destine si je mourrais mécréant.","explicationEn":"23. Shall I take other deities to be wrongly worshipped instead of Allah Who created me? If the Merciful intends harm for me, the intercession of these other deities will not avail me at all, nor will they be able to save me from the harm that Allah intended for me if I die as a disbeliever.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"إِنِّي إِذًا لَفِي ضَلَالٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"Je serai alors dans un égarement évident.","tradEn":"Indeed, I would then be in manifest error.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si je les adoptais comme divinités en dehors d’Allah, je commettrai alors une erreur manifeste puisque j’adorerai des êtres qui ne méritent pas d’être adorés et je délaisserai l’adoration de Celui qui mérite d’être adoré.","explicationEn":"24. If I have to take them as deities besides Allah I would be in clear error as I would have worshipped a being that is not deserving of worship and I would have omitted worshipping the Being Who is deserving thereof.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"إِنِّي آمَنْتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ فَاسْمَعُونِ","tradPropre":"[Mais] je crois en votre Seigneur. Ecoutez-moi donc».","tradEn":"Indeed, I have believed in your Lord, so listen to me.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô mon peuple, je crois en mon Seigneur et votre Seigneur à tous, écoutez-moi donc. Je ne me soucie pas de vos menaces de mort. Or les siens le tuèrent et Allah le fit entrer au Paradis.","explicationEn":"25. O my people, I have accepted both my and your Lord, so listen to me. I do not care about the threats of murder that you make. But his people insisted on killing him and Allah entered him into Paradise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"قِيلَ ادْخُلِ الْجَنَّةَ  قَالَ يَا لَيْتَ قَوْمِي يَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Alors, il [lui] fut dit: «Entre au Paradis». Il dit: «Ah si seulement mon peuple savait!","tradEn":"It was said, \"Enter Paradise.\" He said, \"I wish my people could know","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Après sa mort, tué par son peuple.","explicationUnanime":"On lui dit afin de l’honorer après son martyr: Entre au Paradis. Lorsqu’il y entra et vit les délices qu'il contient,*il souhaita que son peuple qui le traita de menteur et le tua sache que ses péchés lui ont été pardonnés et de quelle manière son Seigneur l’a honoré, afin qu’ils aient la foi comme lui a eu la foi et soient rétribués aussi généreusement que lui.","explicationEn":"27. It was said in honour of this man after his people killed him: Enter Paradise after you are killed as a martyr. When he entered it and saw the delight therein, he said longingly: If only my people who denied and killed me knew about the forgiveness of sins that I obtained and what my Lord has honoured me with, they would have believed like how I believed and they would have attained a reward similar to mine.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"بِمَا غَفَرَ لِي رَبِّي وَجَعَلَنِي مِنَ الْمُكْرَمِينَ","tradPropre":"...en raison de quoi mon Seigneur m'a pardonné et mis au nombre des honorés».","tradEn":"Of how my Lord has forgiven me and placed me among the honored.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On lui dit afin de l’honorer après son martyr: Entre au Paradis. Lorsqu’il y entra et vit les délices qu'il contient,*il souhaita que son peuple qui le traita de menteur et le tua sache que ses péchés lui ont été pardonnés et de quelle manière son Seigneur l’a honoré, afin qu’ils aient la foi comme lui a eu la foi et soient rétribués aussi généreusement que lui.","explicationEn":"27. It was said in honour of this man after his people killed him: Enter Paradise after you are killed as a martyr. When he entered it and saw the delight therein, he said longingly: If only my people who denied and killed me knew about the forgiveness of sins that I obtained and what my Lord has honoured me with, they would have believed like how I believed and they would have attained a reward similar to mine.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"۞ وَمَا أَنْزَلْنَا عَلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ مِنْ جُنْدٍ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ وَمَا كُنَّا مُنْزِلِينَ","tradPropre":"Et après lui Nous ne fîmes descendre du ciel aucune armée. Nous ne voulions rien faire descendre sur son peuple.","tradEn":"And We did not send down upon his people after him any soldiers from the heaven, nor would We have done so.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pour anéantir son peuple, Nous n’avons pas eu besoin de soldats parmi les anges que Nous faisons descendre du Ciel. Leur cas fut plus facile pour Nous puisque Nous avons décidé qu’ils seront anéantis par un cri venant du Ciel et par les anges chargés d’abattre le châtiment.","explicationEn":"28. In order to destroy his people who had denied and killed him, I did not need an army of angels to be sent down from the sky. Their matter was much easier than that for Me. I had decreed that their destruction will be by a blast from the sky and not by sending down the angels of punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"إِنْ كَانَتْ إِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَاحِدَةً فَإِذَا هُمْ خَامِدُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce ne fut qu'un seul Cri et les voilà éteints.","tradEn":"It was not but one shout, and immediately they were extinguished.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Leur fin n’eut lieu que l’espace d’un seul cri qui les foudroya et ne laissa personne parmi eux, tel un feu qui était ardent et qui s’éteignit soudainement sans laisser de trace.","explicationEn":"29. Thus the incident of the destruction of his people was simply one blast which we sent upon them and they fell down with nothing remaining. Their example is like that of a fire that was burning and then was extinguished, leaving behind no trace.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"يَا حَسْرَةً عَلَى الْعِبَادِ  مَا يَأْتِيهِمْ مِنْ رَسُولٍ إِلَّا كَانُوا بِهِ يَسْتَهْزِئُونَ","tradPropre":"Hélas pour les esclaves [les humains]! Jamais il ne leur vient de messager sans qu'ils ne s'en raillent.","tradEn":"How regretful for the servants. There did not come to them any messenger except that they used to ridicule him.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : quelle tristesse pour les hommes !","explicationUnanime":"Que le regret et la contrition des serviteurs dénégateurs seront grands le Jour de la Résurrection lorsqu’ils verront le châtiment. Dans le bas monde, aucun messager ne venait à eux de la part d’Allah sans qu’ils ne le tournent en dérision. Par conséquent, ils seront pleins de regrets le Jour de la Résurrection pour les manquements dont ils ont fait preuve à l’égard d’Allah.","explicationEn":"30. Alas for those servants who denied, and how regretful will their situation be on the day of resurrection when they will see the punishment. That is because in the world, whenever any Messenger from Allah came to them, they used to mock at and ridicule him. Their outcome will therefore be regret on the day of resurrection for the neglect of their duty to Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"أَلَمْ يَرَوْا كَمْ أَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِنَ الْقُرُونِ أَنَّهُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ لَا يَرْجِعُونَ","tradPropre":"Ne voient-ils pas combien de générations avant eux Nous avons fait périr? Lesquelles ne retourneront jamais parmi eux.","tradEn":"Have they not considered how many generations We destroyed before them - that they to them will not return?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces dénégateurs qui raillent les messagers ne voient-ils pas dans les peuples qui les ont précédés une leçon à méditer? Ces peuples sont morts et ne retourneront plus à la vie dans ce bas monde. Ils sont plutôt partis à la rencontre de leurs œuvres et Allah les rétribuera selon leur nature.","explicationEn":"31. Did these people who deny and ridicule the messengers not see a lesson in those nations who preceded them? They passed away and did not return to the world a second time. Rather they met the actions they had sent ahead and Allah will recompense them for that.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"وَإِنْ كُلٌّ لَمَّا جَمِيعٌ لَدَيْنَا مُحْضَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et tous sans exception comparaîtront devant Nous.","tradEn":"And indeed, all of them will yet be brought present before Us.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tous les peuples, sans exception, comparaîtront devant Nous le Jour de la Résurrection, après qu’ils aient été ressuscités, afin que Nous les rétribuions pour leurs œuvres.","explicationEn":"32. All nations, without exception, will be brought before Me on the Day of Resurrection after they are resurrected for Me to give them the recompense for their actions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"وَآيَةٌ لَهُمُ الْأَرْضُ الْمَيْتَةُ أَحْيَيْنَاهَا وَأَخْرَجْنَا مِنْهَا حَبًّا فَمِنْهُ يَأْكُلُونَ","tradPropre":"Une preuve pour eux est la terre morte, à laquelle Nous redonnons la vie, et d'où Nous faisons sortir des grains dont ils mangent.","tradEn":"And a sign for them is the dead earth. We have brought it to life and brought forth from it grain, and from it they eat.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le signe de la réalité de la Ressuscitation, adressé aux dénégateurs, est cette terre sèche et aride sur laquelle Nous faisons descendre la pluie du Ciel. Nous y faisons alors pousser des variétés de plantes et de grains qui nourrissent les gens. Celui qui fait revivre cette terre en y faisant descendre la pluie et en y faisant pousser des plantes a le pouvoir de faire revivre les morts et de les ressusciter.","explicationEn":"33. A sign for those who deny the resurrection that the resurrection is true is this dry and barren land, on which I sent down rain from the sky and I grew therein various types of plants and produced various kinds of grains for people to eat. The One Who gave life to this earth by sending down the rain and bringing out the plants, is able to give life to and resurrect the dead.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلْنَا فِيهَا جَنَّاتٍ مِنْ نَخِيلٍ وَأَعْنَابٍ وَفَجَّرْنَا فِيهَا مِنَ الْعُيُونِ","tradPropre":"Nous y avons mis des jardins de palmiers et de vignes et y avons fait jaillir des sources,","tradEn":"And We placed therein gardens of palm trees and grapevines and caused to burst forth therefrom some springs -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons placé sur cette terre, que Nous avons abreuvée de pluie, des vergers de palmiers et de vignes et nous y avons fait jaillir des sources d’eau qui l’irriguent.","explicationEn":"34. We have placed in this earth, on which I sent down rain, gardens of date palms and grapes; and I caused springs of water to gush forth to irrigate them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"لِيَأْكُلُوا مِنْ ثَمَرِهِ وَمَا عَمِلَتْهُ أَيْدِيهِمْ  أَفَلَا يَشْكُرُونَ","tradPropre":"afin qu'ils mangent de Ses fruits et de ce que leurs mains ont produit. Ne seront-ils pas reconnaissants?","tradEn":"That they may eat of His fruit. And their hands have not produced it, so will they not be grateful?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceci, afin que les gens mangent des fruits de ces vergers la quantité dont Allah leur a fait don, sans qu’ils n’aient eu à fournir d’efforts. Ne se montreront-ils pas reconnaissants pour tous Ses bienfaits en L’adorant Seul et en croyant en Ses messagers?","explicationEn":"35. So that people can eat of the fruits of those gardens that Allah has blessed them with and for which they did not make any effort. Do they not thank Allah, Who gave them all of that out of His bounty and mercy for them, by worshipping Him alone and having faith in His messengers?!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"سُبْحَانَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ الْأَزْوَاجَ كُلَّهَا مِمَّا تُنْبِتُ الْأَرْضُ وَمِنْ أَنْفُسِهِمْ وَمِمَّا لَا يَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Louange à Celui qui a créé tous les couples de ce que la terre fait pousser, d'eux-mêmes, et de ce qu'ils ne savent pas!","tradEn":"Exalted is He who created all pairs - from what the earth grows and from themselves and from that which they do not know.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que soit sanctifié Allah qui créa des variétés de plantes et d’arbres, d’êtres humains (hommes et femmes) ainsi que d’autres créatures terrestres, marines et autres encore que les gens ne connaissent pas.","explicationEn":"36. Glory be to Allah Who created the various types of plants and trees, and of the souls of people, as He created males and females, and other creations of Allah that people do not know of on land, sea and other places.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"وَآيَةٌ لَهُمُ اللَّيْلُ نَسْلَخُ مِنْهُ النَّهَارَ فَإِذَا هُمْ مُظْلِمُونَ","tradPropre":"Et une preuve pour eux est la nuit. Nous en écorchons le jour et ils sont alors dans les ténèbres.","tradEn":"And a sign for them is the night. We remove from it the [light of] day, so they are [left] in darkness.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"La preuve de l'Unicité d'Allah adressée aux gens est que Nous faisons diminuer la lumière du jour et que Nous installons progressivement la nuit en éloignant le jour. C’est alors que les gens se retrouvent dans l’obscurité.","explicationEn":"37. An indication for people of Allah’s Oneness is that I take away the daylight as the day draws to an end, bringing the night, as the day withdraws from it, until the people are in complete darkness.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"وَالشَّمْسُ تَجْرِي لِمُسْتَقَرٍّ لَهَا  ذَالِكَ تَقْدِيرُ الْعَزِيزِ الْعَلِيمِ","tradPropre":"et le soleil court vers un gîte qui lui est assigné; telle est la détermination du Tout Puissant, de l'Omniscient.","tradEn":"And the sun runs [on course] toward its stopping point. That is the determination of the Exalted in Might, the Knowing.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Un autre signe de l’Unicité d’Allah est que le soleil se déplace vers un lieu qui lui est fixé, qu’Allah connaît, sans le dépasser. Ceci a été déterminé par le Puissant à qui personne ne tient tête, le Connaisseur à qui rien des affaires de Ses créatures n’échappe.","explicationEn":"38. A sign for them of Allah’s Oneness is this sun that runs to a point that Allah knows and does not go beyond that. That determination is the determination of the Mighty, who is not challenged by anyone, the Knower from Whom nothing of His creation is hidden.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"وَالْقَمَرَ قَدَّرْنَاهُ مَنَازِلَ حَتَّىٰ عَادَ كَالْعُرْجُونِ الْقَدِيمِ","tradPropre":"Et la lune, Nous lui avons déterminé des phases jusqu'à ce qu'elle devienne comme la palme vieillie.","tradEn":"And the moon - We have determined for it phases, until it returns [appearing] like the old date stalk.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Un autre signe encore de l’Unicité d’Allah est cette lune que Nous faisons apparaitre sous une forme différente chaque nuit. Elle commence petite puis grandit puis se réduit au point d’être aussi fine, courbée qu’une branche de palmier veille et rabougrie.","explicationEn":"39. A sign for them indicating His Oneness, (may He be glorified), is this moon for which I have determined phases each night. It begins small then becomes big and then small again until it becomes similar to a twisted, old date stalk, in it appearing as thin, curved, yellow and old.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"لَا الشَّمْسُ يَنْبَغِي لَهَا أَنْ تُدْرِكَ الْقَمَرَ وَلَا اللَّيْلُ سَابِقُ النَّهَارِ  وَكُلٌّ فِي فَلَكٍ يَسْبَحُونَ","tradPropre":"Le soleil ne peut rattraper la lune, ni la nuit devancer le jour; et chacun vogue dans une orbite.","tradEn":"It is not allowable [i.e., possible] for the sun to reach the moon, nor does the night overtake the day, but each, in an orbit, is swimming.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les signes du soleil, de la lune, de la nuit et du jour sont déterminés par Allah et ne dépassent pas le temps ou le lieu qu’Il leur a déterminé. Ainsi, ni le soleil ne peut rattraper la lune afin de modifier sa trajectoire et de faire disparaitre sa lueur, ni la nuit ne peut précéder le jour et commencer avant le moment qui lui a été fixé. Toutes ces créatures soumises ainsi que d’autres astres et galaxies, possèdent leurs propres parcours déterminés et sauvegardés par Allah.","explicationEn":"40. These signs; the sun moon, night and day, each are predetermined by Allah's divine arrangement/determination and do not surpass what has been determined for them. The sun cannot catch up with the moon to change its course or take away its light, and nor can the night outpace the day and enter upon it before its time ends. All these creations, subservient or not, such as stars and galaxies, have their own courses as per Allah’s determination and protection.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"وَآيَةٌ لَهُمْ أَنَّا حَمَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ فِي الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُونِ","tradPropre":"Et un (autre) signe pour eux est que Nous avons transporté leur descendance sur le bateau chargé;","tradEn":"And a sign for them is that We carried their forefathers in a laden ship.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Un autre signe de l’Unicité d’Allah et des bienfaits dont Il comble Ses serviteurs est que Nous avons transporté les descendants d’Adam qui ont été sauvé du Déluge à l’époque de Noé dans un bateau chargé de créatures d’Allah, un couple de chaque créature.","explicationEn":"41. Another sign for them of Allah’s Oneness and of His favour to His servants is that I carried those who were saved from the flood from the progeny of Adam in the time of Noah in the ship that was filled with Allah’s creations. Allah carried therein a pair of every species.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"وَخَلَقْنَا لَهُمْ مِنْ مِثْلِهِ مَا يَرْكَبُونَ","tradPropre":"et Nous leur créâmes des semblables sur lesquels ils montent.","tradEn":"And We created for them from the likes of it that which they ride.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L’un des signes que Nous leur adressons de l’Unicité d’Allah et des bienfaits dont Il fait don à Ses serviteurs est que Nous leur avons créé des vaisseaux semblables au bateau de Noé.","explicationEn":"42. A sign for them of Allah’s Oneness and His favour to His servants is that I created for them, like the ship of Noah, conveyances and some types of animals on which they can travel long distances.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"وَإِنْ نَشَأْ نُغْرِقْهُمْ فَلَا صَرِيخَ لَهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْقَذُونَ","tradPropre":"Et si Nous le voulons, Nous les noyons; pour eux alors, pas de secoureur et ils ne seront pas sauvés,","tradEn":"And if We should will, We could drown them; then no one responding to a cry would there be for them, nor would they be saved","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si Nous avions voulu les noyer, Nous les aurions noyés et personnes n’aurait eu le pouvoir de les sauver si Nous avions pris une telle décision.","explicationEn":"43. If I wished to drown them I would have done so. There would be no one to help them if I wished to drown them and there would be no one to rescue them if they drowned by My command and decree.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا رَحْمَةً مِنَّا وَمَتَاعًا إِلَىٰ حِينٍ","tradPropre":"sauf par une miséricorde de Notre part, et à titre de jouissance pour un temps.","tradEn":"Except as a mercy from Us and provision for a time.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Sauf si Nous voulons leur faire miséricorde et les faire retourner à leur vie afin qu’ils jouissent de celle-ci pour un temps déterminé qu’ils ne peuvent prolonger, puissent-ils en déduire un enseignement et avoir la foi.","explicationEn":"44. Except if I have mercy on them by rescuing them from drowning and restoring them to enjoy until a specified time that they will not go beyond, so that they take a lesson and have faith.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمُ اتَّقُوا مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِيكُمْ وَمَا خَلْفَكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Et quand on leur dit: «Craignez ce qu'il y a devant vous et ce qu'il y a derrière vous afin que vous ayez la miséricorde»!...","tradEn":"But when it is said to them, \"Beware of what is before you and what is behind you; perhaps you will receive mercy...\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque l’on dit à ces polythéistes qui refusent de croire: Prenez garde aux évènements terribles que vous vivrez dans l’au-delà et prenez garde au bas monde que vous quitterez [tôt ou tard], dans l'espoir qu’Allah vous fasse la faveur de Sa miséricorde. Seulement, ils ne voulurent pas suivre cette recommandation et s’en détournèrent avec insouciance.","explicationEn":"45. When these idolaters who turn away from faith are told: Beware of what you are going towards in the Hereafter and its difficulties, and beware of the world behind you, in the hope that Allah will favour you with His mercy, they do not comply with that but they turn away from it without any care.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"وَمَا تَأْتِيهِمْ مِنْ آيَةٍ مِنْ آيَاتِ رَبِّهِمْ إِلَّا كَانُوا عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِينَ","tradPropre":"Or, pas une preuve ne leur vient, parmi les preuves de leur Seigneur sans qu'ils ne s'en détournent.","tradEn":"And no sign comes to them from the signs of their Lord except that they are from it turning away.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"A chaque fois que parviennent à ces polythéistes entêtés, les signes d’Allah démontrant Son Unicité et le fait qu’Il mérite d’être adoré Seul, ils s’en détournent et ne leur accordent aucune importance.","explicationEn":"46. Whenever Allah’s signs indicating to His Oneness and His being deserving of being worshipped alone came to these idolaters, they used to turn away from it without taking heed.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمْ أَنْفِقُوا مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللَّهُ قَالَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لِلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنُطْعِمُ مَنْ لَوْ يَشَاءُ اللَّهُ أَطْعَمَهُ إِنْ أَنْتُمْ إِلَّا فِي ضَلَالٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"Et quand on leur dit: «Dépensez de ce qu'Allah vous a attribué», ceux qui ont mécru disent à ceux qui ont cru: «Nourrirons-nous quelqu'un qu'Allah aurait nourri s'Il l'avait voulu? Vous n'êtes que dans un égarement évident».","tradEn":"And when it is said to them, \"Spend from that which Allāh has provided for you,\" those who disbelieve say to those who believe, \"Should we feed one whom, if Allāh had willed, He would have fed? You are not but in clear error.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque l’on dit à ces entêtés: Aidez les pauvres et les nécessiteux avec les richesses qu’Allah vous a données, ils répondent avec arrogance aux croyants: Allons-nous nourrir ceux qu'Allah aurait nourris s'Il avait voulu? Nous ne nous opposons pas à Sa volonté. Ô croyants, vous êtes manifestement dans l’erreur et éloignés de la vérité.","explicationEn":"47. When these stubborn ones are told: Assist the poor and the needy with the wealth that Allah has provided you with, they disapprovingly reply saying to those who have faith: Shall we feed those whom Allah could feed if He wanted to?! So we do not go against His will. You, O believers, are simply in clearly error and far off from the truth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"وَيَقُولُونَ مَتَىٰ هَاذَا الْوَعْدُ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صَادِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Et ils disent: «A quand cette promesse si vous êtes véridiques?»","tradEn":"And they say, \"When is this promise, if you should be truthful?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les mécréants qui rejettent, traitent de mensonge et excluent la réalité de la Ressuscitation disent: Quand aura donc lieu cette Ressuscitation si ce que vous prétendez est véridique, ô croyants?","explicationEn":"48. The disbelievers who deny the resurrection say in denial of it and regarding it as far-fetched: When is this resurrection if you, O believers, are true in your claim that it is to occur?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"مَا يَنْظُرُونَ إِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَاحِدَةً تَأْخُذُهُمْ وَهُمْ يَخِصِّمُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils n'attendent qu'un seul Cri qui les saisira alors qu'ils seront en train de disputer.","tradEn":"They do not await except one blast which will seize them while they are disputing.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Le soufflement dans la Corne, annonçant la Résurrection, qui surprendra et foudroiera tous les vivants.","explicationUnanime":"Ces gens-là attendent que le premier souffle dans la Trompe les surprenne, tandis qu’ils seront distraits par leurs préoccupations terrestres comme le négoce, l’irrigation de leurs récoltes, le soin de leur élevage et d’autres activités.","explicationEn":"49. But all these deniers of resurrection who regard it as far-fetched are waiting for is the first blast when it is blown into the trumpet, which will suddenly overtake them while they are in their worldly concerns of buying, selling, irrigating and herding and other worldly concerns.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"فَلَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ تَوْصِيَةً وَلَا إِلَىٰ أَهْلِهِمْ يَرْجِعُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils ne pourront donc ni faire de testament, ni retourner chez leurs familles.","tradEn":"And they will not be able [to give] any instruction, nor to their people can they return.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque ce cri les surprendra, ils ne pourront se formuler des recommandations les uns aux autres ni retourner dans leurs demeures et rejoindre leurs familles. Ils mourront plutôt en pratiquant les activités durant lesquelles ils auront été surpris.","explicationEn":"50. When this blast surprises them they will not be able to make a bequest for one another, and they will not be able to return to their homes and families. Instead, they will die whilst they are in these worldly concerns of theirs.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"وَنُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ فَإِذَا هُمْ مِنَ الْأَجْدَاثِ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمْ يَنْسِلُونَ","tradPropre":"Et on soufflera dans la Trompe, et voilà que, des tombes, ils se précipiteront vers leur Seigneur,","tradEn":"And the Horn will be blown; and at once from the graves to their Lord they will hasten.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ensuite, on soufflera une seconde fois pour marquer la Ressuscitation et ils sortiront alors tous rapidement de leurs tombes pour comparaître devant leur Seigneur qui leur demandera des comptes et les rétribuera.","explicationEn":"51. The trumpet will be blown a second time for the resurrection, and suddenly they will all come out of their graves rushing towards their Lord for the reckoning and recompense.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا يَا وَيْلَنَا مَنْ بَعَثَنَا مِنْ مَرْقَدِنَا   هَاذَا مَا وَعَدَ الرَّحْمَانُ وَصَدَقَ الْمُرْسَلُونَ","tradPropre":"en disant: «Malheur à nous! Qui nous a ressuscités de là où nous dormions?» C'est ce que le Tout Miséricordieux avait promis; et les Messagers avaient dit vrai.","tradEn":"They will say, \"O woe to us! Who has raised us up from our sleeping place?\" [The reply will be], \"This is what the Most Merciful had promised, and the messengers told the truth.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Cette dernière phrase sera, selon certains commentateurs, prononcée par les croyants ou les anges.","explicationUnanime":"Ces mécréants qui nient la réalité de la Ressuscitation diront avec regret: Que notre perte est grande! Qui donc nous a ressuscités de nos tombes? On leur répondra alors: Ceci est la réalisation irrémédiable de la promesse d’Allah et les messagers ont été véridiques lorsqu’ils vous l’ont transmise.","explicationEn":"52. These disbelievers who deny the resurrection will say in regret: What loss is ours! Who is it that has raised us from our grave? They will be given a response to their question: This is what Allah promised and will definitely occur. The messengers spoke the truth in the message of their Lord that they conveyed in this regard.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"إِنْ كَانَتْ إِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَاحِدَةً فَإِذَا هُمْ جَمِيعٌ لَدَيْنَا مُحْضَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce ne sera qu'un seul Cri, et voilà qu'ils seront tous amenés devant Nous.","tradEn":"It will not be but one blast, and at once they are all brought present before Us.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"La Ressuscitation ne prendra qu’un instant après le second souffle dans la Trompe et voilà que toutes les créatures se rendront auprès de Nous le Jour de la Résurrection afin de rendre des comptes.","explicationEn":"53. The matter of resurrection from the graves will only be an effect of a second blowing of the trumpet and all created things will be presented before us on the Day of Resurrection to give account.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"فَالْيَوْمَ لَا تُظْلَمُ نَفْسٌ شَيْئًا وَلَا تُجْزَوْنَ إِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce jour-là, aucune âme ne sera lésée en rien. Et vous ne serez rétribués que selon ce que vous faisiez.","tradEn":"So today [i.e., the Day of Judgement] no soul will be wronged at all, and you will not be recompensed except for what you used to do.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le jugement sera équitable ce jour-là et vous ne subirez pas d’injustice, ô serviteurs, par l’addition de mauvaises œuvres ou la soustraction de bonnes œuvres. Vous ne serez rétribués qu’en conséquence de ce que vous faisiez dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"54. Judgement will be passed with fairness on that day and you, O servants, will not be wronged in the least by an increase of your bad deeds or a reduction in your good deeds. You will simply be given the full recompense for what you used to do in the worldly life.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ أَصْحَابَ الْجَنَّةِ الْيَوْمَ فِي شُغُلٍ فَاكِهُونَ","tradPropre":"Les gens du Paradis seront, ce jour-là, dans une occupation qui les remplit de bonheur;","tradEn":"Indeed the companions of Paradise, that Day, will be amused in [joyful] occupation -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les gens du Paradis seront distraits et ne penseront pas à d’autres personnes qu'eux-mêmes, en raison des délices éternels et du succès qu’ils remporteront. Ils en jouiront alors avec bonheur.","explicationEn":"55. The people of Paradise on this day, which is the day of resurrection, will be preoccupied from thinking about others, because of the permanent bliss and supreme success they will see. They will be enjoying that happily.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"هُمْ وَأَزْوَاجُهُمْ فِي ظِلَالٍ عَلَى الْأَرَائِكِ مُتَّكِئُونَ","tradPropre":"eux et leurs épouses sont sous des ombrages, accoudés sur les divans.","tradEn":"They and their spouses - in shade, reclining on adorned couches.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils profiteront des literies avec leurs épouses sous les ombrages étendus du Paradis.","explicationEn":"56. They and their spouses will be comfortably sitting on couches under lush shades in Paradise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-57.html"},{"numVerset":57,"texteArabe":"لَهُمْ فِيهَا فَاكِهَةٌ وَلَهُمْ مَا يَدَّعُونَ","tradPropre":"Là ils auront des fruits et ils auront ce qu'ils réclameront,","tradEn":"For them therein is fruit, and for them is whatever they request [or wish]","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Dans ce Paradis, ils auront droit à des variétés agréables de fruits: raisins, figues et grenades. Ils auront également droit à tous les plaisirs qu’ils désirent et à toutes sortes de délices. Tout ce qu’ils demanderont leur sera donc accordé.","explicationEn":"57. In this Paradise they will have various types of wholesome fruits such as grapes, figs and pomegranates and they will have any type of delight or bliss that they ask for. Whatever they ask for they will get.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036057","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-56.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-58.html"},{"numVerset":58,"texteArabe":"سَلَامٌ قَوْلًا مِنْ رَبٍّ رَحِيمٍ","tradPropre":"«Salâm» [paix et salut]! Parole de la part d'un Seigneur Très Miséricordieux.","tradEn":"[And] \"Peace,\" a word from a Merciful Lord.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"En plus de tous ces délices, ils seront salués par un Seigneur qui est miséricordieux envers eux. Lorsqu’Il les saluera, ils connaîtront la paix absolue et auront comme réponse une salutation qui n’est surpassée par aucune autre.","explicationEn":"58. Over and above this bliss they will have peace that they will get, as a statement from a Lord Who is merciful to them. When He will greet them with peace they will attain peace and safety from all sides and they will obtain the greeting that no other greeting can surpass.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036058","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-57.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-59.html"},{"numVerset":59,"texteArabe":"وَامْتَازُوا الْيَوْمَ أَيُّهَا الْمُجْرِمُونَ","tradPropre":"«O injustes! Tenez-vous à l'écart ce jour-là!","tradEn":"[Then He will say], \"But stand apart today, you criminals.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On dira aux polythéistes le Jour de la Résurrection: Distinguez-vous des croyants car il ne convient pas qu’ils soient avec vous, puisque leur rétribution et la vôtre sont différentes et leurs caractéristiques et les vôtres sont dissemblables.","explicationEn":"59. The idolaters will be told on the day of resurrection: Step aside from the believers. It is not appropriate for them to be with you because of the disparity in your recompense and theirs and in your attributes and theirs.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036059","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-58.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-60.html"},{"numVerset":60,"texteArabe":"۞ أَلَمْ أَعْهَدْ إِلَيْكُمْ يَا بَنِي آدَمَ أَنْ لَا تَعْبُدُوا الشَّيْطَانَ  إِنَّهُ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"Ne vous ai-Je pas engagés, enfants d'Adam, à ne pas adorer le Diable? Car il est vraiment pour vous un ennemi déclaré,","tradEn":"Did I not enjoin upon you, O children of Adam, that you not worship Satan - [for] indeed, he is to you a clear enemy -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô descendants d’Adam, Ne vous ai-Je pas recommandé et ordonné, par l’intermédiaire de Mes messagers, de ne pas obéir à Satan en vous rendant coupables de mécréance et de péchés. Satan est certainement pour vous un ennemi qui vous voue une hostilité manifeste. Or comment quelqu’un de raisonnable peut-il obéir à son ennemi déclaré?","explicationEn":"60. Did I not advise and instruct you on the tongues of My messengers and say to you: O children of Adam! Do not follow Satan by committing various types of disbelief and sins. Satan is a clear enemy to you. How can any sensible person follow an enemy of his who has made his enmity clear!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036060","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-59.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-61.html"},{"numVerset":61,"texteArabe":"وَأَنِ اعْبُدُونِي  هَاذَا صِرَاطٌ مُسْتَقِيمٌ","tradPropre":"et [ne vous ai-Je pas engagés] à M'adorer? Voilà un chemin bien droit.","tradEn":"And that you worship [only] Me? This is a straight path.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô descendants d’Adam, Je vous ai ordonné de M’adorer Seul et de ne rien M’associer. M’adorer Seul et M’obéir est le droit chemin qui mène à Mon agrément et à l’entrée au Paradis. Seulement, vous n’avez pas obéi à ce que je vous ai recommandé et ordonné.","explicationEn":"61. I instructed you, O children of Adam, to worship Me alone and not to associate anything as partners to me. Worshipping Me alone and following Me is a straight path that leads to My pleasure and entry into Paradise. But you did not comply with my advice and instruction in that regard.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036061","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-60.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-62.html"},{"numVerset":62,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ أَضَلَّ مِنْكُمْ جِبِلًّا كَثِيرًا  أَفَلَمْ تَكُونُوا تَعْقِلُونَ","tradPropre":"Et il a très certainement égaré un grand nombre d'entre vous. Ne raisonniez-vous donc pas?","tradEn":"And he had already led astray from among you much of creation, so did you not use reason?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Satan a égaré nombre d’entre vous. N’étiez-vous pas pourvus d’une raison qui vous ordonne d’obéir à votre Seigneur et de L’adorer Seul et qui vous avertissait d’obéir à Satan qui est votre ennemi déclaré?","explicationEn":"62. Satan has misled many of you. Did you not have intellects which you could use, and with sound reasoning it would have lead you to obey your Lord and worship only Him (may He be glorified)? And your intellects should have been enough as a safeguard from you following Satan who is your clear enemy.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036062","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-61.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-63.html"},{"numVerset":63,"texteArabe":"هَاذِهِ جَهَنَّمُ الَّتِي كُنْتُمْ تُوعَدُونَ","tradPropre":"Voici l'Enfer qu'on vous promettait.","tradEn":"This is the Hellfire which you were promised.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Voici l’Enfer que l’on vous promettait dans le bas monde en rétribution pour votre mécréance et que vous ne voyiez pas mais aujourd’hui, vous le voyez de vos yeux.","explicationEn":"63. This is Hell, which you were warned against in the world for your disbelief. It was a matter of the Ghaib to you, but today here you can witness it with your own eyes.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036063","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-62.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-64.html"},{"numVerset":64,"texteArabe":"اصْلَوْهَا الْيَوْمَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُونَ","tradPropre":"Brûlez-y aujourd'hui, pour avoir mécru».","tradEn":"[Enter to] burn therein today for what you used to deny.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Entrez-y aujourd’hui et endurez sa chaleur pour votre mécréance durant votre vie dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"64. Enter it today and suffer from its heat remaining therein forever on account of your rejection of Allah in your worldly life.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036064","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-63.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-65.html"},{"numVerset":65,"texteArabe":"الْيَوْمَ نَخْتِمُ عَلَىٰ أَفْوَاهِهِمْ وَتُكَلِّمُنَا أَيْدِيهِمْ وَتَشْهَدُ أَرْجُلُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوا يَكْسِبُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce jour-là, Nous scellerons leurs bouches, tandis que leurs mains Nous parleront et que leurs jambes témoigneront de ce qu'ils avaient accompli.","tradEn":"That Day, We will seal over their mouths, and their hands will speak to Us, and their feet will testify about what they used to earn.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce jour-là, Nous scellerons leurs bouches et les rendrons muets, les rendant incapables de nier leur mécréance et leurs péchés. Ce seront leurs mains qui Nous parlerons de ce qu’elles ont fait dans le bas monde et leurs pieds des péchés vers lesquels ils se rendaient.","explicationEn":"65. Today, I will seal their mouths and they will become mute not able to deny the disbelief and sins they committed. Their hands will speak to us about what they did in the world. Their feet will testify about the sins they perpetrated and walked towards.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036065","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-64.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-66.html"},{"numVerset":66,"texteArabe":"وَلَوْ نَشَاءُ لَطَمَسْنَا عَلَىٰ أَعْيُنِهِمْ فَاسْتَبَقُوا الصِّرَاطَ فَأَنَّىٰ يُبْصِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et si Nous voulions, Nous effacerions leurs yeux et ils courront vers le chemin. Mais comment alors pourront-ils voir?","tradEn":"And if We willed, We could have obliterated their eyes, and they would race to [find] the path, and how could they see?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si Nous voulions les priver de vue, Nous le ferions et lorsqu’ils se précipiteront vers le pont Şirâṭ afin de le traverser et d’entrer au Paradis, ils en seront alors incapables.","explicationEn":"66. If I had willed to take away their sight I would have done so and they will not be able to see, just as I sealed their mouths and they were not able to speak. They would have then rushed towards the path to cross over it into Paradise, but it is unlikely that they will cross over when their sight is gone.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036066","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-65.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-67.html"},{"numVerset":67,"texteArabe":"وَلَوْ نَشَاءُ لَمَسَخْنَاهُمْ عَلَىٰ مَكَانَتِهِمْ فَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوا مُضِيًّا وَلَا يَرْجِعُونَ","tradPropre":"Et si Nous voulions, Nous les métamorphoserions sur place; alors ils ne sauront ni avancer ni revenir.","tradEn":"And if We willed, We could have deformed them, [paralyzing them] in their places so they would not be able to proceed, nor could they return.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si Nous voulions changer leur apparence et les figer sur des pattes, Nous le ferions et ils seraient incapables de quitter leurs places: ni d’avancer ni de reculer.","explicationEn":"67. If I had willed to alter their form and make them sit on their feet I would have altered their form and made them sit on their feet, and they will not be able to move from their place nor will they be able to move forward nor backward.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036067","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-66.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-68.html"},{"numVerset":68,"texteArabe":"وَمَنْ نُعَمِّرْهُ نُنَكِّسْهُ فِي الْخَلْقِ  أَفَلَا يَعْقِلُونَ","tradPropre":"A quiconque Nous accordons une longue vie, Nous faisons baisser sa forme. Ne comprendront-ils donc pas?","tradEn":"And he to whom We grant long life We reverse in creation; so will they not understand?","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Si bien qu’il retrouve l’état de faiblesse qui était le sien à sa naissance.","explicationUnanime":"Celui parmi les gens dont Nous allongeons la durée de vie, Nous le faisons retourner à un état de faiblesse. Ne réfléchissent-ils pas et ne s'aperçoivent-ils pas que cette demeure n’est pas une demeure éternelle et que seul l’au-delà en est une?","explicationEn":"68. Whoever’s life I extend by lengthening his lifespan, I return him to the stage of weakness. Do they not think with their intellect and understand that this abode is not one of permanence and immortality and that the everlasting abode is that of the Hereafter!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036068","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-67.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-69.html"},{"numVerset":69,"texteArabe":"وَمَا عَلَّمْنَاهُ الشِّعْرَ وَمَا يَنْبَغِي لَهُ  إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكْرٌ وَقُرْآنٌ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"Nous ne lui (à Muhammad) avons pas enseigné la poésie; cela ne lui convient pas non plus. Ceci n'est qu'un rappel et une Lecture [Coran] claire,","tradEn":"And We did not give him [i.e., Prophet Muḥammad (ﷺ)] knowledge of poetry, nor is it befitting for him. It is not but a message and a clear Qur’ān","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Réponse évidente aux païens de la Mecque qui prétendaient que le Prophète était un poète.","explicationUnanime":"Nous n’avons pas appris de poésie à Muħammad et il ne lui convient pas d’apprendre la poésie, car elle n’est pas compatible avec sa nature. Pourquoi le traitez-vous donc de poète? Nous ne lui avons enseigné qu’un rappel et un Coran clair pour celui qui le médite.","explicationEn":"69. I did not teach Muhammad (peace be upon him) poetry and nor is that appropriate for him, because it is not his nature and his disposition does not demand it so that you can claim that he is a poet. What I have taught him is only a admonition and a clear Qur’ān for those who ponder over it. It is not poetry.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036069","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-68.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-70.html"},{"numVerset":70,"texteArabe":"لِيُنْذِرَ مَنْ كَانَ حَيًّا وَيَحِقَّ الْقَوْلُ عَلَى الْكَافِرِينَ","tradPropre":"pour qu'il avertisse celui qui est vivant et que la Parole se réalise contre les mécréants.","tradEn":"To warn whoever is alive and justify the word [i.e., decree] against the disbelievers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous lui avons enseigné cela afin qu’il avertisse ceux qui possèdent un cœur clairvoyant, puisque ce sont eux qui tirent profit du Coran, et que le châtiment soit prononcé contre les mécréants, car la révélation du Coran aura explicité l’argument contre eux et le Message leur sera parvenu. Ils n’auront alors plus aucune excuse pour justifier leur mécréance.","explicationEn":"70. To warn whose hearts are alive and they still have insight, for they are the ones who will benefit from it, And to establish the punishment against the disbelievers by making our signs manifest to them leaving them with no excuse.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036070","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-69.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-71.html"},{"numVerset":71,"texteArabe":"أَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا أَنَّا خَلَقْنَا لَهُمْ مِمَّا عَمِلَتْ أَيْدِينَا أَنْعَامًا فَهُمْ لَهَا مَالِكُونَ","tradPropre":"Ne voient-ils donc pas que, parmi ce que Nos mains ont fait, Nous leur avons créé des bestiaux dont ils sont propriétaires;","tradEn":"Do they not see that We have created for them from what Our hands have made, grazing livestock, and [then] they are their owners?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ne voient-ils pas que Nous leur avons créé des bestiaux qu’ils possèdent et dont ils disposent selon ce que requièrent leurs intérêts?","explicationEn":"71. Have they not seen that I have created livestock for them, and they control the affairs of that livestock by doing with it whatever they require?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036071","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-70.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-72.html"},{"numVerset":72,"texteArabe":"وَذَلَّلْنَاهَا لَهُمْ فَمِنْهَا رَكُوبُهُمْ وَمِنْهَا يَأْكُلُونَ","tradPropre":"et Nous les leur avons soumis: certains leur servent de monture et d'autres de nourriture;","tradEn":"And We have tamed them for them, so some of them they ride, and some of them they eat.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils sont à leur disposition et leur sont soumis. C’est ainsi qu’ils se servent de certaines de ces bêtes comme montures et bêtes de trait, tandis qu’ils mangent la viande de certaines autres.","explicationEn":"72. I have made the livestock serviceable for them and made it submissive to them; they ride on the backs of some and transport their loads, and they also consume some of its meat.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036072","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-71.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-73.html"},{"numVerset":73,"texteArabe":"وَلَهُمْ فِيهَا مَنَافِعُ وَمَشَارِبُ  أَفَلَا يَشْكُرُونَ","tradPropre":"et ils en retirent d'autres utilités et des boissons. Ne seront-ils donc pas reconnaissants?","tradEn":"And for them therein are [other] benefits and drinks, so will they not be grateful?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils y trouvent d’autres utilisations que le fait de les monter et de manger de leur viande. Ils exploitent ainsi leurs laines et leurs poils à partir desquels ils fabriquent des literies et des vêtements, en plus de boire de leur lait. Ne seront-ils pas reconnaissants envers Allah qui leur a fait la faveur de tels bienfaits et de bien d’autres encore?","explicationEn":"73. They also have benefits in the livestock other than just riding and consuming its meat i.e. its wool, bristles, fur and value, which they use to make spreads and clothing. They can also drink of its milk. So, will they not show gratitude to Allah who has blessed them with these favours, and others?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036073","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-72.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-74.html"},{"numVerset":74,"texteArabe":"وَاتَّخَذُوا مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ آلِهَةً لَعَلَّهُمْ يُنْصَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et ils adoptèrent des divinités en dehors d'Allah, dans l'espoir d'être secourus...","tradEn":"But they have taken besides Allāh [false] deities that perhaps they would be helped.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les polythéistes adoptent des divinités en dehors d’Allah qu’ils adorent afin qu’elles les secourent et les sauvent du châtiment d’Allah.","explicationEn":"74. The idolaters have taken other deities instead of Allah whom they worship, hoping that they will help them and save them from the punishment of Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036074","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-73.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-75.html"},{"numVerset":75,"texteArabe":"لَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ نَصْرَهُمْ وَهُمْ لَهُمْ جُنْدٌ مُحْضَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Celles-ci ne pourront pas les secourir, elles formeront au contraire une armée dressée contre eux.","tradEn":"They are not able to help them, and they [themselves] are for them soldiers in attendance.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : mais celles-ci ne pourront secourir leurs adorateurs, alors même qu’elles assisteront à leur jugement (ou : à leur supplice).","explicationUnanime":"Ces divinités qu’ils ont adoptées ne peuvent se secourir elles-mêmes ni secourir ceux qui les adorent en dehors d’Allah. Eux et leurs idoles seront tous châtiés et chaque camp se désavouera de l’autre.","explicationEn":"75. Those deities that they have taken are not able to help themselves, let alone help whoever worships them instead of Allah. The worshippers, together with their idols, will all be brought to the punishment but will all protest innocence from one another.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036075","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-74.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-76.html"},{"numVerset":76,"texteArabe":"فَلَا يَحْزُنْكَ قَوْلُهُمْ  إِنَّا نَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّونَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Que leurs paroles ne t'affligent donc pas! Nous savons ce qu'ils cachent et ce qu'ils divulguent.","tradEn":"So let not their speech grieve you. Indeed, We know what they conceal and what they declare.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, ne sois pas triste lorsqu’ils te disent que tu n’es pas un messager, que tu es un poète ou qu’ils te lancent d’autres accusations. Nous connaissons les accusations qu’ils lancent comme celles qu’ils dissimulent. Rien ne nous en échappe et Nous les rétribuerons en conséquence.","explicationEn":"76. O Messenger! Do not let their statements grieve you: that you have not been sent as a messenger, or that you are a poet, and other slander they fire towards you. Indeed, I know what they say privately and publicly, nothing is hidden from Me and I will requite them for it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036076","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-75.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-77.html"},{"numVerset":77,"texteArabe":"أَوَلَمْ يَرَ الْإِنْسَانُ أَنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُ مِنْ نُطْفَةٍ فَإِذَا هُوَ خَصِيمٌ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"L'homme ne voit-il pas que Nous l'avons créé d'une goutte de sperme? Et le voilà [devenu] un adversaire déclaré!","tradEn":"Does man not consider that We created him from a [mere] sperm-drop - then at once he is a clear adversary?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L’être humain, qui nie la réalité de la Ressuscitation après la mort, ne se rappelle-t-il pas que Nous l’avons créé de sperme puis qu’il est passé par plusieurs étapes avant de naître et de grandir. Ensuite, il est devenu avide de polémique et de controverses. Ne voit-il pas que cela prouve que la Ressuscitation est possible?","explicationEn":"77. Does the human who rejects the resurrection after death not ponder that I created him from semen, then he went through different phases until he was born and developed, turning into an argumentative and quarrelling creation? Does he not ponder over that to conclude that resurrection is possible?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036077","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-76.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-78.html"},{"numVerset":78,"texteArabe":"وَضَرَبَ لَنَا مَثَلًا وَنَسِيَ خَلْقَهُ  قَالَ مَنْ يُحْيِي الْعِظَامَ وَهِيَ رَمِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Il cite pour Nous un exemple, tandis qu'il oublie sa propre création; il dit: «Qui va redonner la vie à des ossements une fois réduits en poussière?»","tradEn":"And he presents for Us an example and forgets his [own] creation. He says, \"Who will give life to bones while they are disintegrated?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque le mécréant invoque les ossements défraichis comme preuve de l’impossibilité de la Ressuscitation et dit « Qui les rendra tels qu’ils étaient? », il oublie et ignore qu’il a été créé à partir du néant.","explicationEn":"78. This disbeliever is heedless and ignorant when he uses decayed bones to prove the impossibility of resurrection, saying, “Who will resurrect us?” whilst having forgotten his own creation from non-existence.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036078","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-77.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-79.html"},{"numVerset":79,"texteArabe":"قُلْ يُحْيِيهَا الَّذِي أَنْشَأَهَا أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ  وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ خَلْقٍ عَلِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Celui qui les a créés une première fois, leur redonnera la vie. Il Se connaît parfaitement à toute création.","tradEn":"Say, \"He will give them life who produced them the first time; and He is, of all creation, Knowing.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : et dont le pouvoir de création est sans limite.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Muħammad, réponds-lui: C’est Celui qui a créé ces os défraichis qui les fera revivre. Celui qui les crée à partir du néant n’est pas impuissant lorsqu’il s’agit de leur redonner la vie. Allah connait chaque créature et rien de ce qui la concerne ne Lui échappe.","explicationEn":"79. O Muhammad! Say to him in reply: “Whoever created these bones in the first place will bring them back to life, because the one who created them initially is not incapable of returning life to them; He (may He be glorified) is the knower of everything, nothing is hidden from Him.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036079","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-80.html"},{"numVerset":80,"texteArabe":"الَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِنَ الشَّجَرِ الْأَخْضَرِ نَارًا فَإِذَا أَنْتُمْ مِنْهُ تُوقِدُونَ","tradPropre":"c'est Lui qui, de l'arbre vert, a fait pour vous du feu, et voilà que de cela vous allumez.","tradEn":"[It is] He who made for you from the green tree, fire, and then from it you ignite.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, c’est Lui qui fit de l’arbre vert et humide, un combustible lorsque vous voulez allumer un feu. Celui qui réunit deux opposés, l’humidité de l’arbre vert et le feu qui le consume, est capable de faire revivre les morts.","explicationEn":"80. The being who has made for you, O people, lush green trees from which you are able to extract fire by igniting them. So the being who combined two opposites: the moisture of the green trees and the fire ignited from them, is also capable of reviving the dead.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036080","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-79.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-81.html"},{"numVerset":81,"texteArabe":"أَوَلَيْسَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ بِقَادِرٍ عَلَىٰ أَنْ يَخْلُقَ مِثْلَهُمْ  بَلَىٰ وَهُوَ الْخَلَّاقُ الْعَلِيمُ","tradPropre":"Celui qui a créé les cieux et la terre ne sera-t-Il pas capable de créer leur pareil? Oh que si! et Il est le grand Créateur, l'Omniscient.","tradEn":"Is not He who created the heavens and the earth Able to create the likes of them? Yes, [it is so]; and He is the Knowing Creator.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Celui qui créa les Cieux et la Terre malgré leur immensité n’est-Il pas capable de faire revivre les gens après les avoir fait mourir? Si, Il en est parfaitement capable. Il est le Grand Créateur qui crée toutes les créatures, Celui qui les connaît toutes parfaitement, sans que rien les concernant ne Lui échappe.","explicationEn":"81. Is not the one who created the heavens and the earth despite their grandeur, also capable of bringing the dead back to life, after causing their death? Of course! He is definitely capable of it; He is the creator who created all creations and He knows them all, so nothing is hidden from Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036081","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-80.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-82.html"},{"numVerset":82,"texteArabe":"إِنَّمَا أَمْرُهُ إِذَا أَرَادَ شَيْئًا أَنْ يَقُولَ لَهُ كُنْ فَيَكُونُ","tradPropre":"Quand Il veut une chose, Son commandement consiste à dire: «Sois», et c'est.","tradEn":"His command is only when He intends a thing that He says to it, \"Be,\" and it is.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsqu’Allah veut faire exister quelque chose, il Lui suffit de lui dire « Sois » et ce qu’il voulait alors faire exister, existe aussitôt. Ceci est également valable lorsqu’Il veut faire vivre, mourir ou ressusciter.","explicationEn":"82. The authority and prestige of Allah is such that when He intends to create something, all He says to it is “Be!” and so it happens as He intends it. His intending to give life, cause death, and resurrect is also like that.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036082","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-81.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-36-verset-83.html"},{"numVerset":83,"texteArabe":"فَسُبْحَانَ الَّذِي بِيَدِهِ مَلَكُوتُ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَإِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ","tradPropre":"Louange donc, à Celui qui détient en Sa main la royauté sur toute chose! Et c'est vers Lui que vous serez ramenés.","tradEn":"So exalted is He in whose hand is the realm of all things, and to Him you will be returned.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Qu’Allah soit sanctifié et élevé au-dessus de l’impuissance que Lui attribuent les polythéistes. Il est Celui qui possède toute chose et en dispose comme Il le veut. Les clés de toute chose sont dans Sa main et c’est auprès de Lui Seul que vous retournerez dans l’au-delà afin qu’Il vous rétribue pour vos œuvres.","explicationEn":"83. So Allah is glorified and free of the incapability the idolators ascribe to Him. He is the one to whom belongs total authority over everything and He does as He wishes with it; the keys to everything are in His Hands and you shall all return to Him in the Hereafter, where He will requite you over your deeds.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"036083","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-82.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-1.html"}]};